        { "$comment": "P69 round 4 (lane cs): GNU `mode(M)` replaces the declared type by the type of a named machine mode (`int x __attribute__((mode(DI)));` is 8 bytes on gcc 13.3.0 and clang 18.1.3). REFUSED BY NAME until the modes are implemented: MEASURED before this row, the attribute was warned as unknown and the object kept the size its specifiers spell (4), silently different from every reference.", "names": ["mode"], "effect": "unsupported", "reason": "it replaces the declared type by the type of the named machine mode, and this compiler does not implement machine modes" },
